# 12. Scanning Multiple Authorized Targets

Suppose a lab contains:

```text
192.168.56.101
192.168.56.102
192.168.56.103
```

A script can process them one at a time.

```python
import subprocess

targets = [
    "192.168.56.101",
    "192.168.56.102",
    "192.168.56.103"
]

for target in targets:
    print(f"Scanning {target}")

    result = subprocess.run(
        ["nmap", "-sV", target],
        capture_output=True,
        text=True
    )

    print(result.stdout)
```

### Concept

```text
Target 1 → Scan → Result
Target 2 → Scan → Result
Target 3 → Scan → Result
```

