# 13. Why Input Validation Matters

Never blindly execute arbitrary user input as a shell command.

Unsafe concept:

```python
subprocess.run(user_input, shell=True)
```

This can create command-injection risks.

Better:

```python
subprocess.run(
    ["nmap", "-sV", target],
    shell=False
)
```

Here, the executable and arguments are passed separately.

### Golden Rule

> **Treat target input as untrusted data.**

